### Tiles: seven tensors

Own tiles 0..99 then rival 100..199. For cell `c`, `x=c%10`, `y=c/10`, source is `farm.tiles[y][x]`; never transpose x/y.

| Tensor | Rust type / row shape | Source and complete write rule |
|---|---|---|
| `tile_kind` | i64 [200] | null→EMPTY; string `LOCKED`→LOCKED; object kind WEED/PLANT/COOP/PASTURE→2/3/4/5; unknown representation fails |
| `tile_crop` | i64 [200] | PLANT's recognized crop→1..5; all other tiles 0 |
| `tile_animal` | i64 [200] | recognized animal on compatible COOP/PASTURE→1..3; no animal→0; malformed/unknown animal fails |
| `tile_cell` | i64 [200] | c on both farms, row-major 0..99 |
| `tile_role` | i64 [200] | own=0, rival=1 |
| `tiles_int` | i64 [200,7] | channels below, exact |
| `tiles_float` | f32 [200,15] | channels below, one f64→f32 cast |

Let P mean kind PLANT and A mean animal != NONE; day/step come from the validated public clock. Required fields on applicable tiles fail if missing or wrong type; explicit -1 means none, not a missing key. **(Claude review R2)** Tile objects must have exactly the engine-produced key set for their shape: take the sets from the engine constructors (`new_plant`, `new_animal`, `{"kind": structure}` on animal death at `lib.rs:4287`, `{"kind":"WEED"}`, build `{"kind":"COOP"|"PASTURE"}`) and pin them in a test that scans every tile of every official-fixture state. Stale plant keys on a non-plant, animal keys on a non-animal tile, `"animal": null`, or any unknown key are **rejected** (`ObserveErrorKind::State`), not ignored. Every integer tile field, including `pending_care_bonus` (engine `map_i64`/`set_i64`), must be a JSON integer that fits i64; fractional values are rejected. Inapplicable outputs are zero by construction. Consequence: every admitted state is legacy-reconstructible, so the oracle claim needs no "engine-shaped only" carve-out.

